 "note": "AN OMITTED PENDING COUNT ON 2.1.266 MEANS ZERO, NOT UNKNOWN. The turn-end record here carries no pendingBackgroundAgentCount at all, and on a harness at or above 2.1.241 that is how the binary writes an empty set: 236 of 300 measured turn-end records carry a positive integer, 64 omit the key, and none carries a null or a zero. So the turn really ended and exactly one done toast is correct. Below 2.1.241 the field never existed, and there an absent key really is unknown, which is what registry_read.trusts_pending_count gates. This file was originally named e_pending_field_absent_answers_unknown and expected nothing; see superseded_expectation for why that was wrong.",
