  "old_note": "NO DONE TOAST, AND THE REASON IS UNKNOWN RATHER THAN BUSY. The turn-end record here carries no pendingBackgroundAgentCount at all, so transcript_facts answers pending None and rung 8 is unreachable: the resolver must stay silent rather than guess. HONESTY MARKER: this is NOT a pre-2.1.241 install. Every one of the 11,152 versioned records across this corpus reads 2.1.266, so no old-version session exists in the window to sample. 2.1.266 OMITS the field when the count is zero (measured: 355 turn-end records, positive integer or key absent, never null and never 0, interleaved inside one file at one version), and the reader cannot tell that absence from an old binary's. So this fixture exercises exactly the rung an old version would, from a real record, with nothing invented.",
  "why_it_was_wrong": "The old expectation rested on the belief that claude 2.1.266 writes a literal null for pendingBackgroundAgentCount when no agents are pending, so an absent key had to mean a version that never wrote the field at all. Re-measured across 40 recent transcripts, 300 turn_duration records on 2.1.266: 236 carry a positive integer, 64 OMIT THE KEY, zero carry a literal null and zero carry a literal 0. The null was an artifact of jq printing a missing key as null. On a record at or above 2.1.241 the key being absent therefore means ZERO PENDING AGENTS and the turn genuinely finished. This episode is the same shape as c_genuinely_idle_one_toast and must expect the same one done toast."
